Fix a use-after-free in decode_locale_impl with libc++

When the codecvt facet returns partial, decode_locale_impl grows the
output vector and continues, but out_next still points into the buffer
that resize() freed, and the do-while condition does not continue on
partial, so the function returns std::wstring(out.data(), out_next)
built from the dangling pointer. libc++ returns partial for a character
the locale cannot convert (and makes no progress when called again at
it), so decoding non-ASCII text in the C locale read freed memory.

Recompute out_next after the resize, continue the loop on partial, and
treat a partial result that made no progress as an error.

--- a/src/mpt/string_transcode/transcode.hpp
+++ b/src/mpt/string_transcode/transcode.hpp
@@ -1419,10 +1419,18 @@
 			out_next = nullptr;
 			result = facet.in(state, in_begin, in_end, in_next, out_begin, out_end, out_next);
 		}
+		if (result == codecvt_type::partial && in_next == in_begin && out_next == out_begin && out_next != out_end) {
+			// libc++ reports an unconvertible character as partial without
+			// advancing; treat it as the error it is.
+			result = codecvt_type::error;
+		}
 		if (result == codecvt_type::partial || (result == codecvt_type::error && out_next == out_end)) {
+			// out_next points into the buffer that resize() frees.
+			const std::size_t out_pos = out_next - out.data();
 			out.resize(out.size() * 2);
 			in_begin = in_next;
-			out_begin = out.data() + (out_next - out_begin);
+			out_begin = out.data() + out_pos;
+			out_next = out_begin;
 			out_end = out.data() + out.size();
 			continue;
 		}
@@ -1449,7 +1457,7 @@
 		}
 		in_begin = in_next;
 		out_begin = out_next;
-	} while ((result == codecvt_type::error && in_next < in_end && out_next < out_end) || (retry == 2 && in_next < in_end));
+	} while ((result == codecvt_type::partial && in_next < in_end) || (result == codecvt_type::error && in_next < in_end && out_next < out_end) || (retry == 2 && in_next < in_end));
 	return std::wstring(out.data(), out_next);
 }
 
